# The admin session for `npm run check:browser`.
#
# COPY THIS FILE TO `.admin-session` AND FILL IN `cookie`. That file is
# gitignored. Never commit it, never paste its contents into a chat.
#
# WHEN THE GATE SAYS THE SESSION EXPIRED, REDO THESE FIVE STEPS:
#
#   1. Open https://dustinedwards.dustin-edwards.workers.dev/admin in Chrome,
#      signed in as the admin. You should see the cockpit, not the login page.
#   2. F12 for DevTools, then the Application tab.
#   3. Left sidebar: Storage > Cookies > the workers.dev origin.
#   4. Find the row named `__Secure-better-auth.session_token`. Copy the Name
#      cell and the Value cell.
#   5. Paste them below as name=value, on one line, replacing the placeholder.
#
# THE NAME HAS TO BE THERE. A bare value used to be accepted and guessed at: the
# gate asked "does this contain an = sign" to decide whether a name was already
# present, which cannot tell a `name=value` pair from a value carrying base64
# `=` padding. Dustin's 85-character cookie was a bare value, it produced a
# Cookie header with no name, and no server can parse that. The gate refuses a
# nameless value now and says which name it wanted.
#
# Pasting the whole `Cookie:` header from the Network tab works too: the gate
# picks the session cookie out of it by name and ignores the rest.

cookie = __Secure-better-auth.session_token=PASTE_THE_VALUE_HERE

# The DEPLOYED origin the admin cases drive. Not the preview build: sessions
# live in the production KV namespace, so a valid session renders the login page
# against local miniflare storage. Measured, not assumed.
origin = https://dustinedwards.dustin-edwards.workers.dev
